---
/**
 * RTP, MTP and past papers — the free ICAI practice corpus, rendered from
 * `foundationOfficialCorpus` and `foundationAttempts` in
 * src/data/foundation.js. Links only; nothing is re-hosted.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import Badge from '../../components/Badge.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import TrustRow from '../../components/TrustRow.astro';
import {
  foundationAttempts,
  foundationOfficialCorpus,
  foundationPapers,
} from '../../data/foundation.js';

const nextAttempt = foundationAttempts[0];
const rtp = foundationOfficialCorpus.find((r) => r.kind === 'RTP');
const mtp = foundationOfficialCorpus.find((r) => r.kind === 'MTP');
const pastPapers = foundationOfficialCorpus.find((r) => r.kind === 'PastPaper');
---

<Base
  title="CA Foundation RTP, MTP and past papers"
  description="What ICAI's RTPs, MTPs, past papers and model papers are, when each is released relative to an attempt, and where they belong in a revision plan. All free on the BoS portal."
>
  <main class="page">
    <div style="max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <Breadcrumb crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/start-here/' }, { label: 'RTP, MTP & past papers' }]} />

      <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.25;">
        RTP, MTP and past papers, explained
      </h1>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0 24px;">
        <TrustRow attempt={nextAttempt.name} updated="14 Aug 2026" source="ICAI Board of Studies announcements" />
      </div>

      <div class="article">
        <p>
          The single best question bank for CA Foundation is published by the examiner, costs nothing, and
          most students open it three weeks too late. RTPs, MTPs, past papers and model papers are all
          free on the ICAI Board of Studies portal — the same portal your study material comes from, with
          the same free student login.
        </p>

        <Callout kind="pointer" label="Where all of this lives">
          <p>
            <a href="https://boslive.icai.org/" rel="noopener">boslive.icai.org ↗</a> — the BoS Knowledge
            Portal. Log in with your registration number and date of birth; Foundation students see
            Foundation material. Past papers with suggested answers are also on
            {' '}<a href={pastPapers.url} rel="noopener">icai.org ↗</a>, no login needed. Nothing on
            Adhyayan is a re-hosted copy — we link, ICAI publishes.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2>What each one is</h2>
      </div>

      {foundationOfficialCorpus.map((item) => (
        <div class="card card-pad" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <strong style="font-size: 17px;">{item.name}</strong>
            {item.requiresLogin
              ? <Badge kind="login">Requires ICAI login</Badge>
              : <Badge kind="neutral">Open access</Badge>}
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text);">{item.what}</p>
          <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.7;">
            <div><strong style="color: var(--text);">When it lands:</strong> {item.timing}</div>
            <div><strong style="color: var(--text);">How to use it:</strong> {item.useIt}</div>
          </div>
          <div style="margin-top: 12px;">
            <a href={item.url} rel="noopener" style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;">Open on {new URL(item.url).host} ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}

      <div class="article" style="margin-top: 28px;">
        <h2>Timing, relative to your attempt</h2>
        <p>
          Every attempt gets its own RTP and its own two MTP series. They are not interchangeable across
          attempts: the RTP carries the amendments applicable to that specific sitting, which is exactly
          why the RTP of the attempt you are writing matters more than any older one.
        </p>
        <p>
          For {nextAttempt.name} — papers on {nextAttempt.examDates.label},
          {' '}{nextAttempt.session.label.toLowerCase()} — that means the RTP is
          {' '}{rtp.timing.toLowerCase()}. The mock papers follow their own rhythm: {mtp.timing.toLowerCase()}.
        </p>

        <Callout kind="mistake">
          <p>
            Saving the MTPs "until I'm ready". They exist to tell you what ready means, and the answer key
            is worth most when there is still time to act on it. A mock sat at 60% syllabus coverage is a
            diagnostic; a mock sat the week before the exam is only a rehearsal.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2>Where they fit in revision</h2>
        <p>
          A workable ordering, once the syllabus is covered once:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>1. Past papers first.</strong> Take the last three attempts, one paper at a time, and
          attempt before reading the suggested answers. This is where you learn the depth expected.<br />
          <strong>2. RTP during the second revision cycle.</strong> Read the amendment section the day it
          releases; work the question set once you have revised the chapters it draws on.<br />
          <strong>3. MTPs to the clock, in the last few weeks.</strong> Full length, no pauses, in the
          afternoon slot the real papers use. Classify every lost mark afterwards — concept gap, revision
          gap, calculation slip, or time — because the four have different fixes.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the objective papers, the post-mock question worth asking is not "how many did I get wrong"
          but "what did wrong attempts cost me against what skipping would have cost." That arithmetic is
          the whole skill of an OMR paper.
        </p>

        <h2>Per-paper links</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="list-card" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        {foundationPapers.map((paper) => (
          <a class="list-row" href={`/foundation/${paper.slug}/#resources`}>
            <span class="row-num tnum">{String(paper.number).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="row-title">{paper.name}</span>
            <span class="row-meta">Official resources</span>
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="article">
        <h2>Where to go next</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/guides/ca-foundation-exam-pattern/">The exam pattern</a> — the structure your mocks
          should be reproducing, including the {nextAttempt.session.label.toLowerCase()}.<br />
          <a href="/guides/ca-foundation-weightage/">Official section-wise weightage</a> — which chapters
          deserve the questions you have time for.<br />
          <a href="/practice/">Practice sets on Adhyayan</a> — original questions with an explanation on
          every option, to use between the official papers, never instead of them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
